Venera's change to NullMoth's metal2vulkan translator (LGPL-3.0-or-later, packaging/UPSTREAM's TRANSLATOR_COMMIT):
a buffer of records whose address the shader keeps in a local struct and reads back in a helper is an array of those
records. Setup Assistant's "hello" fragment (textFragment) stores its buffer pointers in a Context struct; a helper
loads the Segment buffer's pointer back out of it, reads segments[i] and, through element 0, a member of segments[0].
The pointer reaches the entry's buffer only after its field is forwarded, so the parameter was untyped, and with the
buffer's air.struct_type_info declared, stage-input lowering took the declared struct alone for the whole buffer: the
run-time element index became a struct member index ("owned InBoundsAccessChain violates its access-chain contract").
An untyped buffer with a declared struct layout that the body indexes by a run-time element index, all such accesses
naming one record type of the declared size, is now a runtime array of that record, as it already was when that record
was the only element type the body named (the new body_buf_dynamic_record_element_type in
translator/translator/src/passes/resources/discovery.rs, used in translator/translator/src/passes/stage_input/mod.rs;
test native_record_buffer_read_back_from_a_context_field_is_an_array_of_records). tools/build-translator.sh applies
this patch (patch -p1, from the root of the translator checkout) after 0001 and 0002.

